  "dispositions": [
    {
      "id": "NONFINDING-CHURCH-EMPTY-NAVE-ORDINARY-GENERATION-001",
      "disposition": "An empty nave-axis vector is not admitted by the inspected ordinary generate_structure path when an urban church programme is selected.",
      "trace": "generate_structure calls validate_church_program before plan construction. A present programme must equal URBAN_BRICK_BASILICA, whose nave_bays is four; urban_church::resolve calls resolve_church_assembly only for a present programme. The axis vector is built over 0..nave_bays before it is indexed at zero. Earlier failures can still prevent reaching that index. This is source reasoning only, not an executed generator.",
      "limits": "Other entry paths, mutation or construction within the module, other church dimensions, downstream consumers and the rest of the audit remain open. No claim covers an arbitrary direct private call bypassing the inspected admission.",
      "repair": "not applicable to this bounded suspicion; no implementation",
      "validation": "not performed; source-only evidence verification"
    },
    {
      "id": "NONFINDING-CHURCH-PROVISIONAL-CLERESTORY-ID-001",
      "disposition": "The repeated provisional host ID alone does not establish duplicate retained clerestory hosts after the inspected replacement loop completes successfully.",
      "trace": "For each of four nave bays and two sides the assembly supplies the same owner and slot zero to wall_solid, which appends eight provisional solids with the same ID and matching interface IDs. The window schedule requests each ChurchArcade bay/side. When its lookup selects those newly created distinct wall sources, the first such replacement removes every solid and interface bearing the shared old ID; each successful replacement writes that wall a new host list using a serial-based slot. The loop propagates an error instead of returning its assembly if a lookup or replacement fails. Thus this particular duplicate set is temporary on that conditional successful path, not by itself proof of a surviving duplicate.",
      "limits": "The proof is confined to this provisional set and successful selected-wall replacement; uniqueness against all other geometry and sources, unrelated support IDs, later pipeline mutations, partial internal error state, the actual generated product and all audit outcomes remain open. No generation, audit or runtime observation occurred.",
      "repair": "not applicable to the bounded duplicate-survival suspicion; no implementation",
      "validation": "not performed; source-only evidence verification"
    }
  ],
  "remaining": "Trace source uniqueness and all geometry identities, programme paths, downstream assembly, optional audit, native consumers, historical aliases and every independent lens."
